<title>SOUTH KOREA: S.Korea's NLCF seeks 157,500T of U.S. No.3 corn.</title>
<headline>S.Korea's NLCF seeks 157,500T of U.S. No.3 corn.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1996-09-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's state-run National Livestock Cooperative Federation on Friday invited tenders for a total of 157,500 tonnes of U.S. No.3 yellow corn, traders said.  </p>
<p>Arrival ports were set for Inchon, Pusan, Ulsan and Kunsan.</p>
<p>Deliveries were set by May 25 for position one, June 10 for position two and July 20 for position three.</p>
<p>Details for the tenders are as follows: Position  Amount</p>
<p>	   Shipment</p>
<p>	    (Tonnes)   PNW		 Gulf	 Argentine</p>
<p>   1	52,500 Apr 24-May 13 Apr 5-24 Mar 31-Apr 19</p>
<p>   2	52,500  May 10-29	Apr 21-May 10  Apr 16-May 5</p>
<p>   3	52,500  Jun 19-Jul 8   May 31-Jun 19  May 26-Jun 14</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5651</p>
</text>
